Structural sensitivity. The numerical analysis leaves the dependency structure fixed. Three variants change it. In F, the SE is maintained by either of two external operators. In G, an internal backup B, regenerated by V, can replace the SE for H and V. In H, H and V need at least two of {SE, B1, B2}, with B1 and B2 internal. Table A3 runs them under two readings of the removal step in §10.2: removing each external process alone, and removing them cumulatively, so that the last step has all of them off. Scenario A is repeated for reference.
