The last check removes the hand-built structures. The script generates random dependency structures (3 to 7 components; requirements that are single regenerators or at-least-k groups; two external processes), 5000 per row. The chance that a leaf requirement is an external process (p_ext) and the chance that a requirement is a group (p_group) vary across four rows. For every structure and four removal sets, the simulation agrees with an analytic calculation of the set of components that sustain themselves, in every comparison (20,000 per row). In these structures, then, the simulation computes a property of the dependency structure, and the numerical parameters only set when components fail.
